    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35795" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕtax</span></b> , ācis,
			adj.
		peto, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>catching at</i>, <i>striving after</i>, <i>greedy for</i> any thing; with <i>gen.</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ornatūs petax,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Fulg. Myth. 2, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">potentiae petax,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 3</span></i>
			.—Hence, <i>adv. comp.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕtācĭus</span></b> , <i>more greedily</i>, <i><span class="en">Avien. Progn.
			432</span></i>.</div>
